(subclass ExpectedBehaviorViolationBug SoftwareBug)
(termFormat EnglishLanguage ExpectedBehaviorViolationBug "expected behavior violation bug")
(documentation ExpectedBehaviorViolationBug EnglishLanguage "A &%SoftwareBug
whose discriminating property is that a &%ContentBearingObject records the
specifying agent's &%intendedBehavior for the program prior to the deviation,
and the specifying agent has declared that document.  Adapted from CWE-440
(Expected Behavior Violation) : 'A feature, API, or function does not perform
according to its specification.'")

(=>
  (and
    (instance ?PROG ComputerProgram)
    (programBehavior ?PROG ?INPUT ?ACTUAL)
    (intendedBehavior ?PROG ?INTENDED ?AGENT)
    (not (equal ?ACTUAL ?INTENDED))
    (exists (?DOC ?DECL)
      (and
        (instance ?DOC ContentBearingObject)
        (containsInformation ?DOC (intendedBehavior ?PROG ?INTENDED ?AGENT))
        (instance ?DECL Declaring)
        (agent ?DECL ?AGENT)
        (patient ?DECL ?DOC))))
  (exists (?BUG)
    (and
      (instance ?BUG ExpectedBehaviorViolationBug)
      (bugInProgram ?BUG ?PROG ?AGENT))))
